  "_commit": {
    "id": "5ba02723c2ffabdc100c27eafcedb2797ec8ea25",
    "author": "federicogiorgi <federico.giorgi@gmail.com>",
    "committer": "federicogiorgi <federico.giorgi@gmail.com>",
    "message": "Fix method dispatch, null distribution and numeric edge cases\n\nThree exported functions could not be called the way their own\ndocumentation describes them. gsea(), vulcan.annotate() and\nvulcan.pathways() never resolved 'method' with match.arg(), so calling\nthem without naming a method left the full default vector in place and\nthe later if() saw a condition of length greater than one, which R has\ntreated as an error since 4.2. Every example passes the argument\nexplicitly, which is why the build stayed green while the documented\ndefault was unusable.\n\nnull_gsea() failed whenever a permutation placed the whole set on\nelements of weight zero: the cumulative sum of hits ends at zero, the\nrunning score becomes undefined throughout, and the comparison that\npicks the enrichment score then errors. gsea() has guarded against this\nsince it was written; the null did not. With a set of five among\ntwenty-five elements of which twenty weigh zero it happens in 29% of\npermutations.\n\nThe branch in gsea() meant to accept a precomputed null keyed by set\nsize tested for a class name that nothing in the package ever assigns,\nso it could not be taken, and the test itself could error when handed a\nmatrix. It now accepts a named list and leaves plain vectors alone.\n\nAlso corrected: corr2p() returned exactly 0 for strong correlations by\nsubtracting a probability from one; kmgformat() prefixed zero with the\ncharacter \"0\", so it rendered \"00\" on any axis pretty() put a zero on;\nval2col() measured the colour scale before centring the data, which\ncollapsed shifted data to a single colour, failed outright on small\nranges, and left the smallest value with no colour at all; and\naverage_fragment_length() was one base long, correlateReads() counting\nits delays from zero.\n\nassay() is now imported from SummarizedExperiment instead of being\npicked up from whatever happened to be attached, and DESCRIPTION uses\nAuthors@R, which BiocCheck had begun reporting as an error.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <nor",
    "time": 1786992740
  },
